rs turned to their benches to freshen up their squads. Norman Bassette made way for Isa Sakamoto , while Lommel United introduced Malick Mbaye in an attempt to find a late consolation. The match became more physical in the final ten minutes, resulting in a yellow card for Lasse Floe in the 82nd minute. In the dying embers of the game, KVC Westerlo managed their lead with composure, making late substitutions including Thomas Van den Keybus and David Amegnaglo to see out the clock. When the referee finally blew the whistle after six minutes of added time, the home side celebrated a comprehensive performance that left their opponents searching for answers."
